      "name": null,
      "problem": "A car travels at $1\\,000$ meters per minute. In kilometers, how far will the car travel in one hour?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the units $\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}},$ and we want to convert this into $\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.$ We're converting two units instead of just one, so we're going to have to multiply by two conversion factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nOne of the conversion factors should change $\\text{m}$ to $\\text{km}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nThe other conversion factor should change $\\text{min}$ into $\\text{hour}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{\\text{hour}}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{m}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}}=\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.\n$$\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The rate given in the problem statement is $1\\,000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}.$\n\n- There are $1\\,000$ meters per kilometer, therefore, there are $\\frac{1}{1\\,000}$ kilometers per meter.\n\n- There are $60$ minutes in one hour.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}} & =1000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{m}}\\cdot 60\\,\\frac{\\text{min}}{\\text{hour}} \\\\  & =1000\\cdot \\frac{1}{1\\,000}\\cdot 60(\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{km}}{\\cancel{\\text{m}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{\\text{hour}}) \\\\  & =60\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{hour}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, a speed of $1\\,000$ meters per minute is equivalent to $60$ kilometers per hour. Thus, the car will travel $60$ kilometers in one hour.",
